+### 6b. Audio: transcript with speakers, and summary (async jobs)
+
+Three routes, all under `Authorization: Bearer <project-key>` (same `401 unauthorized` as `/chat`).
+Both operations are **jobs**: you get a `job_id`, then poll. Jobs live in gateway memory; a job can be read
+only with the project key that created it. Field names are snake_case; every reply is `{ success, data }` or
+`{ success:false, error }`.
+
+**`POST /audio/transcriptions`** — `multipart/form-data` with one part, `file`. The gateway reads the bytes;
+the file name and declared type are ignored.
+
+```bash
+curl -s -X POST http://localhost:3009/audio/transcriptions \
+  -H 'Authorization: Bearer <project-key>' \
+  -F 'file=@call.m4a'
+# → 202 {"success":true,"data":{"job_id":"…","status":"queued"}}
+```
+
+| Status | `error` | When |
+|---|---|---|
+| 400 | `file_required` | Not multipart, or no `file` part |
+| 413 | `file_too_large` | Over `AUDIO_MAX_BYTES` (default 100 MiB). Over 128 MiB the 413 has an empty body, so treat every 413 as too large |
+| 415 | `unsupported_audio` | 0 bytes, or the bytes are not a listed format |
+| 415 | `video_not_allowed` | The container holds a video track |
+| 429 | `busy` | `AUDIO_MAX_CONCURRENT` jobs already running or queued; retry later |
+| 503 | `audio_not_configured` | The provider setting or its key is missing |
+
+Accepted by bytes: M4A/MP4 audio, AAC (ADTS), MP3, WAV, Ogg/Opus, WebM audio, FLAC. AMR is not accepted.
+
+**`POST /audio/summaries`** — `application/json`, at most 5 MiB:
+
+```bash
+curl -s -X POST http://localhost:3009/audio/summaries \
+  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
+  -H 'Authorization: Bearer <project-key>' \
+  -d '{"turns":[{"speaker":1,"text":"…"},{"speaker":2,"text":"…"}]}'
+# → 202 {"success":true,"data":{"job_id":"…","status":"queued"}}
+```
+
+Errors: `400 turns_required` (bad JSON, missing or empty `turns`, or a turn without an integer `speaker` and a
+non-empty string `text`) · `413 body_too_large` · `429 busy` · `503 audio_not_configured`.
+
+**`GET /audio/jobs/:job_id`** — poll every 5 seconds.
+
+```json
+{ "success": true, "data": { "job_id": "…", "kind": "transcription", "status": "running" } }
+```
+
+- `kind`: `transcription` | `summary`. `status`: `queued` | `running` | `done` | `failed`.
+- `done` adds `result`; `failed` adds `error`. A failed job is still HTTP `200`.
+- `404 { "success": false, "error": "job_not_found" }`: unknown, expired, another project's, or lost in a gateway
+  restart. Resubmit.
+- Transcription `result`: `{ provider, model, no_speech, speaker_count, turns:[{speaker,text}], latency_ms }`.
+  `speaker` is an integer from 1, numbered by first appearance; it says nothing about who the person is.
+  No speech is `no_speech: true` with `turns: []`, status `done`.
+- Summary `result`: `{ provider, model, summary, latency_ms }`, plain Thai text.
+- Failed job `error`: `{ "code": "…", "retryable": true|false }`, with `code` one of `provider_timeout`,
+  `provider_failed`, `provider_response_invalid` (all retryable), `provider_rejected_audio`, `output_truncated`
+  (not retryable). A partial transcript or summary is never returned as `done`.
+
 ---
 
 ## 7. Limits (honest)
 
+- **Audio providers are `gemini`, `xai` and `stub`**, chosen by `AUDIO_TRANSCRIBE_PROVIDER` and
+  `AUDIO_SUMMARY_PROVIDER`; with none set, `/audio/*` answers `503 audio_not_configured`. `stub` makes no network call.
+
 - **Web search is not automatic inside `/chat`** — use the `/search/classify` +
   `/search` primitives and feed results into `/chat` yourself.
 - `/search` is backed by **Tavily's free tier** (query-only; no open-proxy/URL fetch).
